(window.MAG=window.MAG||{}).d=(window.MAG.d||{});window.MAG.d["3-toledo-iii"]=[["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p1","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","In the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, in the fourth year of the reign of the most glorious and most pious and to God most faithful Lord Recared the king, on the eighth day before the Ides of May, in the era 627, this holy synod was held in the royal city of Toledo by the bishops of all Spain and Gaul, who are written below.","IN NOMINE DOMINI NOSTRI IESU CHRISTI anno regnante quarto gloriosissimo atque piissimo et deo fidelissimo domno Recaredo rege, die VIII Id. Maiar. era DCXXVII haec sancta synodus habita est in civitate regia Toletana ab episcopis totius Spaniae vel Galliae, qui infra scripti sunt."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p2","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Since for the sincerity of his faith the same most glorious prince had commanded all the pontiffs of his reign to come together into one, that both concerning his conversion and concerning the renewal of the Gothic nation they might exult in the Lord and for so great a gift give thanks to the divine condescension, the aforementioned most holy prince thus addresses the venerable council, saying:","Cum pro fidei suae sinceritate idem gloriosissimus princeps omnes regiminis sui pontifices in unum convenire mandasset, ut tam de eius conversione quam de gentis Gothorum innovatione in domino exultarent et divinae dignationi pro tanto munere gratias agerent, memoratus sanctissimus princeps sic venerandum concilium alloquitur dicens:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p3","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Not unknown I think it to be to you, most reverend priests, that for the sake of restoring the form of ecclesiastical discipline I have called you to the presence of our serenity, and because in the times turned back the imminent heresy in the whole catholic church denied to transact synodical business, God, to whom it pleased through us the barrier of the same heresy to drive away, has admonished the institutes according to ecclesiastical custom to restore. Therefore let it be to you of joyfulness, let it be of gladness, that the canonical custom by our regard, while through our glory to the paternal boundaries it is led back, is seen. First however I admonish equally and exhort that to fastings and vigils and prayers you give attention, that the canonical order, which from priestly senses long and daily oblivion had withdrawn, which our age itself confesses itself not to know, by the divine gift again to you may be opened.","Non incognitum reor esse vobis, reverentissimi sacerdotes, quod propter instaurandam disciplinae ecclesiasticae formam ad nostrae vos serenitatis praesentiam evocaverim, et quia decursis retro temporibus heresis imminens in tota ecclesia catholica agere synodica negotia denegabat, deus, cui placuit per nos eiusdem heresis obicem depellere, admonuit instituta de more ecclesiastico reparare. Ergo sit vobis iocunditatis, sit gaudii, quod mos canonicus prospectu, dum per nostram gloriam ad paternos reducitur terminos. Prius tamen admoneo pariter et exhortor ieiuniis vos et vigiliis atque orationibus operam dare, ut ordo canonicus, quem a sacerdotalibus sensibus detraxerat longa ac diurna oblivio, quam aetas nostra se nescire fatetur, divino vobis rursus dono patefiat."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p4","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","To these things moreover thanks to God and to the most religious prince by the whole council in praises shouting, a three days' fast was thereafter proclaimed.","Ad haec autem gratias deo agentes et religiosissimo principi universo concilio in laudibus acclamante, triduanum est exinde praedicatum ieiunium."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p5","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","But when on the eighth day before the Ides of May in one assembly the priests of God were present and prayer having been offered each of the priests in a fitting place had sat down, behold in their midst the most serene prince stood and himself with the priests of God in prayer participating, by the divine stream thereafter filled began to speak thus, saying:","Sed cum die octavo Id. Maiar. in unum coetum dei sacerdotes adessent et oratione praemissa unusquisque sacerdotum competenti loco resedisset, ecce in medio eorum adfuit serenissimus princeps seque cum dei sacerdotibus orationi communicans, divino deinceps flumine plenus sic alloquendum exorsus est dicens:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p6","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","We do not believe your holiness to be ignorant, in how great a time in the error of the Arians Spain had labored, and not many days after the departure of our father, in which days your blessedness us to the holy catholic faith knew to have been joined, we believe generally great and eternal joy to have had. And therefore, venerable fathers, to this synod to be completed we have gathered you, that for men lately coming to Christ you yourselves may eternal thanks to the Lord bring. Whatever moreover by words before your priesthood by us was to be done concerning our faith and hope, which we bear, in this tome written and presented we make known. Let it be read therefore in your midst and in synodal judgment examined for all succeeding time our glory by the testimony of the same faith adorned may shine forth.","Non credimus vestram latere sanctitatem, quanto tempore in errore Arrianorum laborasset Spania et non multos post discessum genitoris nostri dies, quibus nos vestra beatitudo fidei sanctae catholicae cognovit esse sociatos, credimus generaliter magnum et aeternum gaudium habuisse, et ideo, venerandi patres, ad hanc vos peragendam congregavimus synodum, ut de hominibus nuper advenientibus ad Christum ipsi aeternas domino gratias deferatis. Quicquid vero verbis apud sacerdotium vestrum nobis agendum erat de fide atque spe nostra, quam gerimus, in hoc tomo conscripta atque allegata innotescimus. Relegatur enim in medio vestri et in iudicio synodali examinata per omne succiduum tempus gloria nostra eiusdem fidei testimonio decorata clarescat."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p7","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Received moreover it was by all the priests of God, the tome of the sacrosanct faith being offered by the king, and the notary pronouncing it with clear voice was recited.","Susceptus est autem ab omnibus dei sacerdotibus offerente rege sacrosanctae fidei tomus et pronuntiante notario clara voce recensitus est:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p8","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Although God almighty for the utilities of the peoples the summit of the kingdom to undergo has granted us and the governance of not a few nations to our royal care has entrusted, we remember nevertheless ourselves by the condition of mortals to be bound, nor was it able to serve to error, but to the acknowledgment of faith and to the fellowship of the catholic church we might recall. For there is the whole renowned nation of the Goths and by the genuine manliness of almost all nations esteemed, which although by the depravity of its own teachers from the faith heretofore and from the unity of the catholic church has been segregated, now however by the whole unhappiness of future blessedness otherwise to be merited, unless we to the worship of the true faith we should refer and to our creator with confession of salvation, in which way he worthy himself is, we should please. For which thing by how much with the glory of subjects we are raised up, by so much provident we ought to be in those things which are of God, either our hope to conduct or to the nations to us by God entrusted to consult.","Quamvis deus omnipotens pro utilitatibus populorum regni nobis culmen subire tribuerit et moderamen gentium non paucarum regiae nostrae curae commiserit, meminimus tamen nos mortalium condicione perstringi nec posse famulabatur errori, ad agnitionem fidei et ecclesiae catholicae consortium revocarem. Adest enim omnis gens Gothorum inclita et fere omnium gentium genuina virilitate opinata, quae licet suorum pravitate doctorum a fide hactenus vel unitate ecclesiae fuerit catholicae segregata, toto tamen nunc infelicitatem futurae beatitudinis aliter promereri, nisi nos cultui verae fidei reputemus et conditori nostro salutis confessione, quo dignus ipse est, placeamus. Pro qua re quanto subditorum gloria regali extollimur, tanto providi esse debemus in his, quae a deo sunt vel nostram spem agere vel gentibus nobis a deo creditis consulere."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p9","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Moreover what for so great gifts of benefits to the divine omnipotence we are able to give, when all things are his and of our good things nothing he needs, unless that in him thus with all devotion we believe, just as through the sacred Scriptures he himself to be understood willed and to be believed commanded, that is, that we confess the Father to be, who generated from his own substance a Son to himself coequal and coeternal, not however that he himself the same born unbegotten, but in person another is the Father who generated, another is the Son who was generated, of one however each substance in divinity subsists. And the Holy Spirit by us to be confessed and to be preached is from the Father and the Son to proceed, and with the Father and the Son of one substance to be. The third indeed in the Trinity of the Holy Spirit to be a person, who nevertheless communion has with the Father and the Son in the essence of divinity. This holy Trinity is one God, the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit, by whose goodness of man, although good be created a creature, through the assumed however by the Son of human habit a form from a damned progeny we are reformed to pristine blessedness.","Ceterum quid pro tantis beneficiorum collationibus omnipotentiae divinae valemus tribuere, quando omnia ipsius sint et bonorum nostrorum nihil egeat, nisi ut in eum sic tota devotione credamus, quemadmodum per scripturas sacras se ipse intellegi voluit et credi praecepit, id est, ut confiteamur esse patrem, qui genuerit ex sua substantia filium sibi coaequalem et coaeternum, non tamen, ut ipse idem natus ingenitus, sed persona alius sit pater, qui genuit, alius sit filius, qui fuerit generatus, unius tamen uterque substantiae in divinitate subsistat. Spiritusque sanctus confitendus a nobis et praedicandus est a patre et filio procedere, et cum patre et filio unius esse substantiae. Tertiam vero in trinitate spiritus sancti esse personam, qui tamen communionem habet cum patre et filio in divinitatis essentia. Haec enim sancta trinitas unus est deus, pater et filius et spiritus sanctus, cuius bonitate hominis, licet bona sit condita creatura, per assumptam tamen a filio humani habitus formam a damnata progenie reformamur ad beatitudinem pristinam."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p10","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","But just as of true salvation it is the sign the Trinity in unity and the unity in the Trinity to be understood, so it will be consummated justice, if the same within the universal church we hold and the apostolic unity placed upon the apostolic foundation we guard. You however, priests of God, ought to remember, how greatly hitherto the church of God catholic through Spains by the annoyances of the adverse party has labored, while both the catholics constantly the truth of their faith would hold and defend, and the heretics with more pertinacious animosity to their own perfidy would strive. Me also, as the thing itself looks upon, with the heat of faith inflamed in this the Lord raised up, that the obstinacy of unfaithfulness having been driven away and the fury of discord having been removed, the people who under the name of religion to the same assent, to the communion of his church partaking, which of diverse nations the multitude in the maternal bosom receives and with the breasts of charity nourishes, concerning which the prophet singing it is said: My house the house of prayer shall be called for all nations. For not only the conversion of the Goths to the accumulation of our reward has come, but indeed also of the Suevi a countless multitude, which by heavenly aid to our kingdom we have subjected. By alien although fault into heresy led, by our zeal however to the origin of truth we have recalled.","Sed sicut verae salutis indicium est trinitatem in unitate et unitatem in trinitate sentiri, ita erit consummata iustitia, si eandem intra universalem ecclesiam teneamus et apostolicam unitatem in apostolico positi fundamento servemus. Vos tamen dei sacerdotes meminisse oportet, quanta hucusque ecclesia dei catholica per Spanias aversae partis molestiis laboraverit, dum et catholici constanter fidei suae tenerent ac defenderent veritatem, et heretici pertinaciori animositati propriae niterentur perfidiae. Me quoque, ut res ipsa conspicit, calore fidei accensum in hoc dominus excitavit, ut depulsa obstinatione infidelitatis et discordiae submoto furore populus, qui sub nomine religionis eo assensus concordans eius ecclesiae communioni participatur, quae diversarum gentium multitudinem materno in sinu suscipit et caritatis uberibus nutrit, de qua propheta canente dicitur: Domus mea domus orationis vocabitur omnibus gentibus. Nec enim sola Gothorum conversio ad cumulum nostrae mercedis accessit, quin immo et Suevorum gentis infinita multitudo, quam praesidio caelesti nostro regno subiecimus. Alieno licet vitio in heresim deductam nostro tamen ad veritatis originem studio revocavimus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p11","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Therefore, most holy fathers, these most noble nations, which to the gains of the Lord through us have been applied, as a holy and placable sacrifice by your hands to the eternal God I offer. For it will be to me an unfading crown or joy in the retribution of the just, if these peoples who to unity of the church by our diligence have run, founded in the same and stablished remain. For just as by divine nod it was of our care these peoples to the unity of Christ's church to draw, so let it be of your teachability by catholic dogmas to instruct, that in the whole knowledge of truth instructed they may know wholly and solidly pernicious errors to reject and the true faith's path from charity to retain or to the catholic church's communion with more eager desire to embrace. Moreover just as easily to pardon to have come I trust that which unknowing until now so very dear a nation has erred, so more gravely to be I doubt not, if acknowledged truth with doubting heart they should hold and from the powerful light, which may it be absent, their eyes they should avert.","Proinde, sanctissimi patres, has nobilissimas gentes, quae lucris per nos dominicis applicatae sunt, quasi sanctum et placabile sacrificium per vestras manus aeterno deo offero. Erit enim mihi immarcescibilis corona vel gaudium in retributione iustorum, si hi populi, qui nostra ad unitatem ecclesiae sollertia transcurrerunt, fundati in eadem et stabiliti permaneant. Sicut enim divino nutu nostrae curae fuit hos populos ad unitatem Christi ecclesiam pertrahere, ita sit vestrae docibilitatis catholicis eos dogmatibus instituere, quo in tota cognitione veritatis instructi noverint ex toto ex solido errores perniciosos respuere et verae fidei tramitem ex caritate retinere vel catholicae ecclesiae communionem desiderio avidiori amplecti. Ceterum sicut facile ad veniam pervenisse confido, quod nescia hucusque tam carissima erraverit gens, ita gravius esse non dubito, si agnitam veritatem dubio corde teneant atque a potenti lumine, quod absit, oculos suos avertant."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p12","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Whence very necessary it has appeared to your blessedness in one to convene, holding the faith of the Lord's sentence, which says: Where there shall have been two or three gathered in my name, there I am in their midst. For I believe the blessed divinity of the holy Trinity to this holy council to be present, and therefore as before the sight of God thus in your midst my faith, which I have brought forth, conscious as of the divine sentence saying: I have not hidden your mercy and your truth from the great congregation, and the apostle Paul to Timothy the disciple commanding I have heard: Fight the good fight of faith, lay hold on eternal life, unto which you have been called and have confessed the good confession before many witnesses. True indeed is of our Redeemer the sentence from the Gospel, by which him confessing before men to confess he says before the Father and denying him himself to be denied. For it is expedient for us with mouth to profess that which with heart we believe, according to the heavenly command, by which it is said: With heart indeed belief is unto justice, but with mouth confession is made unto salvation. Therefore just as I anathematize Arius with all his dogmas and accomplices, who the only-begotten Son of God from the paternal substance degenerating from the mass asserted to be, nor, against the same pest of the right faith Arius the holy episcopal synod of three hundred and eighteen wrote, which heretical perversity condemned.","Unde valde pernecessarium esse prospexit vestram in unum convenire beatitudinem, habens sententiae dominicae fidem, qua dicit: Ubi fuerint duo aut tres collecti in nomine meo, ibi ero in medio eorum. Credo enim beatam sanctae trinitatis divinitatem huic sancto interesse concilio, et ideo tamquam ante conspectum dei ita in medio vestri fidem meam, quam protuli conscius admodum sententiae divinae dicentis: Non celavi misericordiam tuam et veritatem tuam a congregatione multa, et apostolum Paulum Timotheo discipulo praecipientem audivi: Certa bonum certamen fidei, appraehende vitam aeternam, in qua vocatus es et confessus bonam confessionem coram multis testibus. Vera est enim redemptoris nostri ex evangelio sententia, qua confitentem se coram hominibus confiteri dicit coram patre et negantem se esse negaturum. Expedit enim nobis id ore profiteri, quod corde credimus, secundum caeleste mandatum, quo dicitur: Corde enim creditur ad iustitiam, ore autem confessio fit ad salutem. Proinde sicut anathematizo Arrium cum omnibus dogmatibus et complicibus suis, qui unigenitum dei filium a paterna degnere massae rebat esse substantiam nec a, quae contra eundem rectae fidei pestem Arrium trecentorum et decem et octo sancta episcopalis scripsit synodus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p13","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","I embrace therefore and I hold the faith of the one hundred and fifty bishops assembled at Constantinople, which Macedonius the substance of the Holy Spirit lessening and from the unity and essence of the Father and the Son by the throat of truth destroyed. The first also Ephesine synod the faith which against Nestorius and his doctrine was published, I believe equally and I honor. Similarly also of the Chalcedonian council the faith, which with full sanctity and erudition against Eutyches and Dioscorus it brought forth, with the whole catholic church reverently I receive. Of all also the orthodox venerable priests the councils, which from the above-written four synods in purity of faith do not dissent, with equal veneration I observe.","Amplector itaque et teneo fidem centum quinquaginta episcoporum Constantinopolim congregatorum, quae Macedonium spiritus sancti substantiam minorantem et a patris et filii unitate et essentia segregantem iugulo veritatis interemit. Prima quoque Ephesina synodus fidem, quae adversus Nestorium eiusque doctrinam lata est, credo pariter et honoro. Similiter et Chalcedonensis concilii fidem, quam plena sanctitate et eruditione adversus Eutychen et Dioscorum protulit, cum omni ecclesia catholica reverenter suscipio. Omnium quoque orthodoxorum venerabilium sacerdotum concilia, quae ab ipsis suprascriptis quattuor synodis fidei puritate non dissonant, pari veneratione observo."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p14","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","Let therefore your reverence hasten this faith of ours to canonical monuments to apply, that by the bishops or religious and the chief men of our nation skillfully the faith, which in the catholic church they have believed, may be read. Which renewed by copies or by their subscriptions strengthened for future times for a testimony of God and of all the faithful keep, that the nations, which in the name of God by royal power we excel, and which having left the ancient error through the anointing of the sacrosanct chrism and the imposition of hand the Paraclete Spirit within the church of God have received, whom one and equal with the Father and the Son confiding and by whose gift in the bosom of the holy catholic church they have been placed.","Properet ergo reverentia vestra fidem hanc nostram canonicis applicare monumentis, ut ab episcopis vel religiosis et gentis nostrae primoribus sollerter fides, quam in ecclesia catholica crediderunt, legatur. Quam renovata metapicibus vel eorum subscriptionibus roboratam futuris olim temporibus in testimonium dei atque omnium fidelium reservate, ut gentes, quas in dei nomine regia potestate praecellimus, et quae relicto antiquo errore per unctionem sacrosancti chrismatis vel manus impositionem paraclitum intra dei ecclesiam perceperunt spiritum, quem unum et aequalem cum patre et filio confidentes eiusque dono in sinu ecclesiae sanctae catholicae collocatae sunt."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p15","Incipit Toletana Synodus Tertia XX Duorum Episcoporum in Qua Arriana Heresis in ","But if some of them this belief and our holy confession not to believe shall have willed, the wrath of God with eternal anathema let them receive, that from their destruction to the faithful might be joy, to the unfaithful might be for an example. To this indeed my confession of the holy Scriptures and of the councils constitutions consenting and by divine testimony with all simplicity of heart I have subscribed.","Quodsi eorum aliqui hanc credulitatem et sanctam confessionem nostram minime credere voluerint, iram dei cum anathemate aeterno percipiant, ut de interitu suo fidelibus gaudium, infidelibus sint in exemplum. Huic vero confessioni meae sanctarum scripturarum et conciliorum constitutionibus consentiens et testimonio divino tota cordis simplicitate subscripsi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p16","Incipit Fides a Sancto Niceno Concilio","We believe in one God the Father almighty, of all things visible and invisible the creator, and in one Lord Jesus Christ the Son of God from the Father born only-begotten, that is, from the substance of the Father, God from God, light from light, true God from true God, born not made, homoousion to the Father, that is of the same with the Father substance, through whom all things were made, which in heaven and which in earth, who for us and for our salvation descended and was incarnate, man was made, suffered and rose again on the third day, and ascended into heaven, from there to come to judge the living and the dead, and in the Holy Spirit. Those moreover who say, there was when he was not, and before he was born he was not, and that from non-existing things he was made or from another substance or subsistence they say him to be or convertible the Son of God, the catholic and apostolic church anathematizes.","Credimus in unum deum patrem omnipotentem omnium visibilium et invisibilium conditorem et in unum dominum Iesum filium dei de patre natum unigenitum, hoc est, de substantia patris, deum ex deo, lumen ex lumine, deum verum ex deo vero, natum non factum, homousion patris, hoc est eiusdem cum patre substantiae, per quem omnia facta sunt, quae in caelo et quae in terra, qui propter nos et propter nostram salutem descendit et incarnatus est, homo factus passus est et resurrexit tertia die et ascendit in caelos, inde venturus iudicare vivos et mortuos, et in spiritum sanctum. Eos autem, qui dicunt, erat, quando non erat, et antequam nasceretur, non erat, et quia ex nullis exsistentibus factus est aut ex alia substantia vel subsistentia dicunt esse aut convertibilem filium dei, anathematizat catholica et apostolica ecclesia."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p17","Item Sancta Fides, Quam Exposuerunt Patres CL Consona Voce, Qui Constantinopolim","LIKEWISE THE HOLY FAITH, WHICH THE FATHERS ONE HUNDRED AND FIFTY WITH CONSONANT VOICE SET FORTH, WHO AT CONSTANTINOPLE WERE GATHERED.",""],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p18","Item Sancta Fides, Quam Exposuerunt Patres CL Consona Voce, Qui Constantinopolim","We believe in one God the Father almighty, maker of heaven and earth, of all things visible and invisible the creator, and in one Lord Jesus Christ the Son of God only-begotten, from the Father born before all ages, God from God, light from light, true God from true God, born not made, homoousion to the Father, that is, of the same with the Father substance, through whom all things were made, both which in heaven and which in earth, who for us and for our salvation descended and was incarnate of the Holy Spirit and of Mary the virgin, man was made, suffered under Pontius Pilate and was buried, and on the third day rose again, ascended into heaven, sits at the right hand of the Father, again to come with glory to judge the living and the dead, of whose kingdom there shall be no end, and in the Holy Spirit the Lord and life-giver from the Father proceeding, with the Father and the Son to be adored and to be glorified, who spoke through the prophets, one catholic and apostolic church. We confess one baptism into remission of sins, we look for the resurrection of the dead, the life of the future age. Amen.","Credimus in unum deum patrem omnipotentem factorem caeli et terrae, visibilium omnium et invisibilium conditorem et in unum dominum Iesum Christum filium dei unigenitum, ex patre natum ante omnia saecula, deum ex deo, lumen ex lumine, deum verum ex deo vero, natum non factum, homousion patri, hoc est, eiusdem cum patre substantiae, per quem omnia facta sunt, et quae in caelo et quae in terra, qui propter nos et propter nostram salutem descendit et incarnatus est de spiritu sancto et Maria virgine, homo factus passus est sub Pontio Pilato et sepultus est et tertia die resurrexit, ascendit in caelos, sedit ad dexteram patris, iterum venturus cum gloria iudicare vivos et mortuos, cuius regni non erit finis, et in spiritum sanctum dominum et vivificatorem ex patre procedentem cum patre et filio adorandum et glorificandum, qui locutus est per prophetas, unam catholicam atque apostolicam ecclesiam. Confitemur unum baptisma in remissionem peccatorum, exspectamus resurrectionem mortuorum, vitam futuri saeculi. Amen."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p19","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","It had sufficed indeed for the most full acknowledgment and confirmation of piety this most cautious and salutary symbol of divine grace. For concerning the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit it teaches perfect doctrine and the Lord's incarnation to those faithfully receiving it manifests. But since those who the preaching of truth to destroy strive, certain novelties of their own heresy bring forth, some indeed the mystery for us wrought of the divine dispensation dare to corrupt and that voice of the virgin birth made to the virgin deny, others a mixture of confessions introducing and one to be the nature of flesh and of divinity insensibly composing, passible of the only-begotten the divine nature with such confusion prodigiously divulge, therefore every against the truth to be opposed from them machine wishing to exclude, the holy and great universal synod the ancient preaching immovable teaching, established principally that the faith of the three hundred and eighteen holy fathers uncontaminated remain. And on account of those who to the Holy Spirit oppose, of the one hundred and fifty fathers a little later time in the city of Constantinople convening concerning the substance of the Holy Spirit handed down doctrine confirms, which also to all they made known, not that in the preceding something was lacking adding, but concerning the Holy Spirit of the same understanding, against those who of his deity the dominion strive to take away, by the testimonies of the Scriptures more fully manifesting. On account of those indeed who the mystery of the dispensation try to corrupt and a mere man to be who of the holy virgin was born impudently divulge, of the most blessed Cyril of the Alexandrian church priest the synodical epistles both to Nestorius and to the others through the East suitable and to himself consenting it receives for the confutation indeed of Nestorian madness, for the interpretation truly of those who with religious zeal of the salutary symbol the understanding seize, by which also the letter of the holy and most blessed of the first see the archbishop Leo to Flavian written of holy record the archbishop for destroying the malice of Eutyches, which to the confession of great Peter agrees and a certain common page existing against those who rightly do not glorify, for the confirmation of the catholic religion evidently it subjoined. For those who into two sons the mystery of the Lord's dispensation to split strive it execrates, and those who passible the divinity of the only-begotten Son of God dare to assert from the council of priests it repels, and those who in the two natures of Christ a mixture or confusion argue it opposes, and who of a heavenly or of any other substance to exist the form of a servant, which for us he assumed, in their madness assert, far it casts out, and those who two indeed before the union natures of the Lord rave, one after the union feign, anathema it makes.","Suffecerat quidem ad plenissimam pietatis agnitionem et confirmationem cautissimum hoc et salutare divinae gratiae symbolum. De patre enim et filio et spiritu sancto doctrinam perfectam edocet et incarnationem dominicam fideliter suscipientibus manifestat. Sed quoniam, qui praedicationem veritatis destruere nituntur, quasdam propriae hereseos novitates partiunt, quidam enim mysterium pro nobis actum divinae dispensationis audent corrumpere et vocem illam virginei partus factam ad virginem denegant, alii temperamentum confusionum inducentes et unam esse naturam carnis et deitatis insensate componentes, passibilem unigeniti divinam naturam tali confusione prodigiose divulgant, idcirco omnem adversus veritatem opponendam ab ipsis machinationem volens excludere sancta et magna universalis synodus antiquam praedicationem immobilem docens, statuit praecipue trecentorum et decem et octo sanctorum patrum fidem incontaminatam manere. Et propter eos, qui spiritui sancto adversantur, centum quinquaginta patrum paulo posteriori tempore in urbe Constantinopolitana convenientium de substantia spiritus sancti traditam doctrinam corroborat, quam etiam illi omnibus insinuaverunt, non quod in praecedentibus aliquid deesset adicientes, sed de spiritu sancto eorundem intellectum, adversus eos, qui deitatis eius dominationem nituntur adimere scripturarum testimoniis plenius manifestantes. Propter eos sane, qui dispensationis mysterium temptant corrumpere et purum hominem esse, qui ex sancta virgine natus est, impudenter divulgant, beatissimi quondam viri Cyrilli Alexandrinae ecclesiae sacerdotis synodicas epistolas tam ad Nestorium quam ad ceteros per orientem congruas et sibi consentientes suscipit ad confutationem quidem Nestorianae amentiae, interpretationem vero eorum, qui religioso zelo salutaris symboli cupiunt intellectum, quibus et epistolam sancti ac beatissimi primae sedis archiepiscopi Leonis ad Flavianum scriptam sanctae recordationis archiepiscopo ad perimendam Euticetis malignitatem, quaeque magni Petri confessioni concordat et communem quandam paginam exsistentem contra eos, qui recte non glorificant ad confirmationem catholicae religionis evidenter subiunxit. Nam eos, qui in duos filios dispensationis dominicae mysterium scindere moliuntur, exsecratur et eos, qui passibilem divinitatem unigeniti filii dei audent asserere, de concilio sacerdotum repellit, et eos, qui in duabus naturis Christi temperamentum vel confusionem argumentantur, adversatur, et qui caelestem aut alterius cuiusque substantiae exsistere formam servi, quam pro nobis assumpsit, insaniendo asserunt, procul abicit, et eos, qui duas quidem ante adunationem naturas domini delirant, unam vero post adunationem confingunt, anathema facit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p20","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Consenting therefore to the holy fathers one and the same Son to confess our Lord Jesus Christ with consonant voice equally we are taught, perfect the same in humanity, true God and true man the same from rational soul and body, according to divinity of one with the Father nature, according to humanity the same of one nature with us, through all things like to us without sin, before ages indeed from the Father born according to divinity, in the last days indeed the same on account of us and on account of our salvation from Mary the virgin the Mother of God according to humanity one and the same Christ the Son the Lord only-begotten in two natures inconfusedly, immutably, indivisibly, inseparably knowing, in nothing of the natures the differences on account of the union to be destroyed, rather the property of each nature being saved and into one person and one state concurring, not into two persons to be divided or to be separated, but one and the same Son only-begotten true God Lord Jesus Christ, just as from the beginning the prophets concerning him, and he himself taught us, and the symbol of the fathers handed down to us.","Consentientes igitur sanctis patribus unum eundemque filium confiteri dominum nostrum Iesum Christum consona voce pariter edocemur, perfectum eundem in humanitate, deum verum et hominem verum eundem ex anima rationali et corpore, secundum divinitatem unius cum patre naturae, secundum humanitatem eundem unius naturae nobiscum, per omnia similem nobis absque peccato, ante saecula quidem ex patre natum secundum divinitatem, novissimis vero diebus eundem propter nos et propter salutem nostram ex Maria virgine dei genetrice secundum humanitatem unum eundemque Christum filium dominum unigenitum in duabus naturis inconfuse, immutabiliter, indivise, inseparabiliter cognoscendo, in nullo naturarum differentias propter unitatem perimendas, magis autem salva utriusque naturae proprietate et in una coeunte persona unoque statu concurrente, non in duabus personis partiendum vel dividendum, sed unum eundemque filium unigenitum deum verum dominum Iesum Christum, sicut ab exordio prophetae de eo, et ipse nos erudivit, et patrum nobis tradidit symbolum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p21","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","These things therefore with all subtlety and diligence by us having been ordered, established the holy and universal synod another faith to none to be allowed to bring forth or to write or to publish or to separate or to teach otherwise. Who moreover dare either to dispose another faith or to bring forth or to hand down another symbol to those wishing to be converted to the knowledge of the truth either from Gentiles or from Jews or from heretics any, if indeed bishops or clerics they shall have been, strangers themselves to be from the episcopate and from the clergy, if truly monks or laymen they shall have been, with anathema to be struck.","His itaque cum omni subtilitate et diligentia a nobis ordinatis, statuit sancta et universalis synodus aliam fidem nulli licere proferre aut scribere aut edere aut separare aut docere aliter. Qui autem audent aut disponere aliam fidem aut proferre aut tradere alium symbolum volentibus converti ad scientiam veritatis vel ex gentibus vel Iudaeis vel hereticis quibuscumque, si quidem aut episcopi aut clerici fuerint, alienos se esse episcopos ab episcopatu et clericos a clero, si vero monachi aut laici fuerint, anathemate feriri."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p22","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","I, Recared the king, this holy and true confession, which through the whole world the catholic church confesses, with heart retaining, with mouth affirming, with my right hand, God protecting, have subscribed.","Ego Recaredus rex fidem hanc sanctam et veram confessionem, quam una per totum orbem catholica confitetur ecclesia corde retinens, ore affirmans, mea dextera deo protegente subscripsi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p23","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","I, Badda the glorious queen, this faith, which I have believed and received, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed.","Ego Badda gloriosa regina hanc fidem, quam credidi et suscepi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p24","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Then it was shouted in the praises of God and in the favor of the prince by the whole council:","Tunc acclamatum est in laudibus dei et in favore principis ab universo concilio:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p25","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","I. Glory to God the Father and to the Son and to the Holy Spirit, whose care it is peace and unity to his holy catholic church to provide.","I. Gloria deo patri et filio et spiritui sancto, cui cura est pacem et unitatem ecclesiae suae sanctae catholicae providere."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p26","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","II. Glory to our Lord Jesus Christ, who at the price of his blood the catholic church from all nations gathered.","II. Gloria domino nostro Iesu Christo, qui pretio sanguinis sui ecclesiam catholicam ex omnibus gentibus congregavit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p27","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","III. Glory to our Lord Jesus Christ, who so illustrious a nation to the unity of the true faith joined and one flock and one shepherd established.","III. Gloria domino nostro Iesu Christo, qui tam illustrem gentem unitati verae fidei copulavit et unum gregem et unum pastorem instituit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p28","IIII. To whom by God eternal merit, if not to the catholic Recared the king?","VIIII. He himself be to God and to all amiable, who so wonderfully God glorified on earth, our Lord Jesus Christ granting, who with God the Father lives and reigns in the unity of the Holy Spirit unto ages of ages.","VIIII. Ipse sit deo et omnibus amabilis, qui tam mirabiliter deum glorificavit in terris praestante domino nostro Iesu Christo, qui cum deo patre vivit et regnat in unitate spiritus sancti in saecula saeculorum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p29","IIII. To whom by God eternal merit, if not to the catholic Recared the king?","IN THE NAME OF OUR LORD JESUS CHRIST LIKEWISE THE CONFESSION OF FAITH OF THE BISHOPS, PRESBYTERS, AND OF THE CHIEF MEN OF THE GOTHIC NATION, WHO BELOW HAVE SUBSCRIBED.","IN NOMINE DOMINI NOSTRI IESU CHRISTI ITEM FIDEI CONFESSIO EPISCOPORUM, PRESBYTERORUM VEL PRIMORUM GOTHICAE GENTIS, QUI INFRA SUBSCRIPSERUNT."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p30","IIII. To whom by God eternal merit, if not to the catholic Recared the king?","But by the whole venerable council instructing and commanding, one of the catholic bishops to the bishops and religious clerics or the elders from the Arian heresy converted began to speak with an address of this kind, saying:","Praecipiente autem universo venerabili concilio atque iubente, unus episcoporum catholicorum ad episcopos et religiosos clericos vel maiores natu ex heresi Arriana conversos eiusmodi allocutione exorsus est dicens:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p31","IIII. To whom by God eternal merit, if not to the catholic Recared the king?","By the care of our office and by the admonition of the most faithful and most glorious prince we are compelled, diligently from your charity to inquire, both what you condemn in the heresy and what within the holy catholic church you believe. For with the psalmist saying we say: Begin to the Lord in confession, it is best and to your salvation it is fitting openly to confess what you believe, and in the hearing of all to anathematize what you reject. Then truly you will be able best of the evangelical and apostolic faith to be made partakers, if the same catholic faith from catholic confession you begin and by your own subscription you strengthen, and just as to God already of good conscience you are known, so also to your neighbor by the assertion of holy faith you may show yourselves. Thus it will be done, that both you of Christ's body to be members you may signify and our littleness nothing doubtful, nothing unfaithful ever of your fraternity may suspect, while it shall have been evident that you the pest of Arian perfidy with all its dogmas, rules, offices, communion, books you condemn, and of the detestable heresy spoiled of contagion, renewed in a certain way within the church of God with the splendid habit of true faith you may shine.","Officii nostri cura et fidelissimi ac gloriosissimi principis admonitione compellimur, diligenter a vestra caritate perquirere, vel quid damnetis in heresi aut quid intra sanctam catholicam credatis ecclesiam. Nam dicente psalmista dicimus: Incipite domino in confessione, optimum est et vestrae saluti conveniens palam confiteri quod creditis, et sub auditu universorum anathematizare quod respuitis. Tunc prorsus optime poteritis evangelicae atque apostolicae fidei participes fieri, si eandem fidem catholicam ex confessione catholica incipiatis vel propria subscriptione firmetis, et sicut deo iam de bonae consensionis cogniti estis conscientia, ita et proximo vos fidei sanctae adstipulatione monstretis. Eo itaque fiet, ut et vos Christi esse corporis membra significetis et nostra exiguitas nihil dubium, nihil infidum umquam de vestra suspicetur fraternitate, dum patuerit vos pestem perfidiae Arrianae cum omnibus dogmatibus, regulis, officiis, communione, codicibus praedamnare ac detestandae hereseos exspoliati contagione, innovati quodammodo intra ecclesiam dei splendido habitu verae fidei clareatis."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p32","IIII. To whom by God eternal merit, if not to the catholic Recared the king?","Then all the bishops together with their clerics and the chief men of the Gothic nation with equal consent said: Although that which your paternity and fraternity from us wishes to hear or to be done, already at the time of our conversion we did, when following our most glorious lord Recared the king on this day to the church we passed over and the Arian perfidy with all its superstitions anathematized equally and cast off, now truly on account of the charity and devotion which both to God and to the holy catholic church we remember ourselves to owe, not only these same things which you seek most promptly to do we hasten, but also if anything yet to the faith agreeable you see and to us with charity you persuade, we will do. For we once for all by the love of the right faith into that devotion have been brought, that everything which more truly by your fraternity to us you open, we hold and with free confession we acknowledge.","Tunc episcopi omnes una cum clericis suis primoresque gentis Gothicae pari consensione dixerunt: Licet hoc, quod paternitas atque fraternitas vestra a nobis cupit audire vel fieri, tam olim conversionis nostrae tempore egerimus, quando secuti gloriosissimum dominum nostrum Recaredum regem hac die ad ecclesiam transivimus et perfidiam Arrianam cum omnibus superstitionibus suis anathematizavimus pariterque abiecimus, nunc vero propter caritatem et devotionem, quam vel deo vel ecclesiae sanctae catholicae meminimus nos debere, non tantum haec eadem, quae petitis promptissime agere properamus, sed et, si qua adhuc congrua fidei esse prospicitis ac nobis caritate persuadetis, faciemus. Nos etenim semel rectae fidei amor in eam devotionem advexit, ut omne, quod nobis verius fraternitate vestra patefacitis, teneamus et libera fateamur confessione."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p33","Anathemas","Therefore everyone who the faith and communion from Arius coming and even to us retained still to hold desires and from all intention of heart does not condemn, let him be anathema.","Omnis ergo, qui fidem et communionem ab Arrio venientem et usque ad nos retentam adhuc tenere desiderat et de tota cordis intentione non damnat, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p34","Anathemas","Whoever the Son of God our Lord Jesus Christ shall have denied from the paternal substance without beginning to be born and to the Father to be equal or consubstantial, let him be anathema.","Quicumque filium dei dominum Iesum Christum negaverit a paterna substantia sine initio genitum et aequalem patri esse vel consubstantialem, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p35","Anathemas","Whoever the Holy Spirit does not believe or shall not have believed from the Father and the Son to proceed, and him shall not have said coeternal to the Father and the Son and consubstantial, let him be anathema.","Quicumque spiritum sanctum non credit aut non crediderit a patre et filio procedere, eumque non dixerit coaeternum esse patri et filio et coessentialem, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p36","Anathemas","Whoever in the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit both the persons does not distinguish and of the one divinity the substance does not acknowledge, let him be anathema.","Quicumque in patre et filio et spiritu sancto et personas non distinguit et unius divinitatis substantiam non agnoscit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p37","Anathemas","Whoever the Son of God our Lord Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit according to divinity than the Father lesser shall have asserted and by grades shall have separated and a creature to be shall have said, let him be anathema.","Quicumque filium dei dominum nostrum Iesum Christum et spiritum sanctum esse iuxta deitatem patre minorem asseruerit et gradibus separaverit creaturamque esse dixerit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p38","Anathemas","Whoever the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit of one substance, omnipotence, eternity to be does not believe, let him be anathema.","Quicumque patrem et filium et spiritum sanctum unius substantiae, omnipotentiae, aeternitatis esse non credit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p39","Anathemas","Whoever the Son of God not to know that which the Father knows shall have said, let him be anathema.","Quicumque nescire filium dei, quae pater sciat, dixerit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p40","Anathemas","Whoever a beginning to the Son of God and to the Holy Spirit shall have assigned, let him be anathema.","Quicumque initium filio dei et spiritui sancto deputaverit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p41","Anathemas","Whoever the Son of God according to his divinity visible or passible shall have dared to profess, let him be anathema.","Quicumque filium dei secundum divinitatem suam visibilem aut passibilem ausus fuerit profiteri, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p42","Anathemas","Whoever the Holy Spirit as the Father and the Son true God and omnipotent to be does not believe, let him be anathema.","Quicumque spiritum sanctum sicut patrem et filium verum deum et omnipotentem esse non credit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p43","Anathemas","Whoever elsewhere the faith and catholic communion besides the church which the Nicene and Constantinopolitan and the first Ephesine and Chalcedonian council decrees hold equally and honor, let him be anathema.","Quicumque alibi fidem et communionem catholicam praeter ecclesiam, quam Niceni et Constantinopolitani et primi Ephesini et Chalcedonensis concilii decreta tenent pariter et honorant, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p44","Anathemas","Whoever the Father and the Son by honor and glory and divinity separates and disjoins, let him be anathema.","Quicumque patrem et filium honore et gloria et divinitate separat et disiungit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p45","Anathemas","Whoever the Son of God and the Holy Spirit with the Father to be glorified and to be honored shall not have believed, let him be anathema.","Quicumque filium dei et spiritum sanctum cum patre non crediderit esse glorificandos et honorandos, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p46","Anathemas","Whoever shall not have said: Glory to the Father and to the Son and to the Holy Spirit, let him be anathema.","Quicumque non dixerit: Gloria patri et filio et spiritui sancto, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p47","Anathemas","Whoever the sacrilege of rebaptizing to be a good work believes or shall have believed, does or shall have done, let him be anathema.","Quicumque rebaptizandi sacrilegium opus bonum esse credit aut crediderit, agere aut egerit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p48","Anathemas","Whoever the detestable book in the twelfth year of King Leovigild by us published, in which is contained the leading over of the Romans to the Arian heresy and in which \"Glory to the Father through the Son in the Holy Spirit,\" which badly by us instituted is contained, this book, if anyone for true shall have held, let him be anathema in eternity.","Quicumque libellum detestabilem XII anno Leobigildi regis a nobis editum, in quo continetur Romanorum ad heresem Arrianam transductio et in quo gloria patri per filium in spiritu sancto, quo male a nobis instituta continetur, hunc libellum, si quis pro vero habuerit, anathema sit in aeternum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p49","Anathemas","For we confess ourselves from the Arian heresy with all heart, all soul, and from all our mind to the catholic church to have been converted. To no one let it be doubtful that we and our successors have erred in the Arian heresy and the evangelical and apostolic faith now within the catholic church have learned. Therefore the holy faith, which our most religious lord made known in the midst of the council and with his hand subscribed, this also we hold, this we confess equally and receive, this in the peoples to preach and to teach we promise.","Confitemur enim nos ex heresi Arriana toto corde, tota anima et de tota mente nostra ad ecclesiam catholicam fuisse conversos. Nulli dubium sit nos nostrosque successores errasse in heresi Arriana et fidem evangelicam atque apostolicam nunc intra ecclesiam catholicam didicisse. Proinde fidem sanctam, quam religiosissimus dominus noster patefecit in medio concilii et manu sua subscripsit, hanc et nos tenemus, hanc confitemur pariter et suscipimus, hanc in populis praedicare atque docere promittimus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p50","Anathemas","This is the true faith, which as the whole church, while through the whole world it holds, the catholic church to be is believed and proved. To whom this faith does not please or shall not have pleased, let him be anathema maranatha in the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.","Haec est vera fides, quam omnis ecclesia, dum per totum mundum tenet ecclesia catholica esse, creditur et probatur. Cui haec fides non placet aut non placuerit, sit anathema maranatha in adventu domini nostri Iesu Christi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p51","Anathemas","Who the faith of the Nicene council and of the Constantinopolitan one hundred and fifty bishops spurns and true to be shall not have said, let him be anathema.","Qui fidem spernit Niceni concilii et Constantinopolitani centum quinquaginta episcoporum veramque esse non dixerit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p52","Anathemas","Who the faith of the first Ephesine synod and of the Chalcedonian does not hold and by them is not delighted, let him be anathema.","Qui fidem Ephesini synodi primi et Chalcedonensis non tenet et ea non delectatur, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p53","Anathemas","Who the councils of all orthodox bishops consonant with the councils of Nicaea, Constantinople, the first Ephesus, and Chalcedon has not received, let him be anathema.","Qui concilia omnium orthodoxorum episcoporum consona conciliorum Niceni, Constantinopolitani, primi Ephesini et Chalcedonensis non recepit, anathema sit."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p54","Anathemas","Therefore this condemnation of the perfidy of Arian communion and of all the councils favoring the Arian heresy with anathema by their own hand we have subscribed.","Proinde damnationem hanc perfidiae communionis Arrianae et omnium conciliorum heresem Arrianam foventium cum anathemate eorum propria manu subscripsimus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p55","Anathemas","The constitutions indeed of the holy councils of Nicaea, Ephesus, and Chalcedon, which with most grateful ear we have heard and with our consent true to be we have proved, from all heart and from all soul and from all our mind we have subscribed, nothing to the knowledge of truth more lucid judging than that the authorities of the above-said councils contain.","Constitutiones vero sanctorum conciliorum Niceni, Ephesini vel Chalcedonensis, quas gratissima aure audivimus et consensione nostra veram esse probavimus, de toto corde et de tota anima et de tota mente nostra subscripsimus, nihil ad cognitionem veritatis lucidius arbitrantes quam supradictorum conciliorum continent auctoritates."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p56","Anathemas","Concerning the Trinity indeed and the unity of the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit, nothing more true than these, nothing more lucid ever can or will be able to be demonstrated; concerning the mystery of the incarnation of the only-begotten Son of God for the salvation of the human race, by which both the true assumption of human nature without sin is proved and remains in him the uncorrupted fullness of divinity, while each nature does not perish and one is made from both, of our Lord Jesus Christ the person, sufficiently plainly in these councils it is proved the truth to be made clear, which by us is believed with all removed doubt.","De trinitate autem et unitate patris et filii et spiritus sancti nihil his verius, nihil lucidius umquam potest vel poterit demonstrari, de mysterio incarnationis unigeniti filii dei pro salute humani generis, quo et vera probatur humanae naturae sine peccati contagione susceptio et permanet incorruptae in eo divinitatis plenitudo, dum haec natura utraque non deperit et una fit ex utraque domini nostri Iesu Christi persona, satis plane in his conciliis probatur patefieri veritas, quae a nobis creditur omni remota dubitatione."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p57","Anathemas","Whoever ever this holy faith shall have tried to deprave, corrupt, change, or from the same faith or catholic communion, which lately we have been by God having mercy made partakers, himself to separate or to dissociate shall have willed, let him be to God and to the whole world by the crime of unfaithfulness in eternity liable. Moreover let the holy catholic church flourish through all the world most peacefully and let it excel in doctrine, holiness, and power. If any within it shall have been and shall have communicated, let them hear at the right hand of the Father placed: Come, blessed of my Father, receive the kingdom which has been prepared for you from the origin of the world. If any indeed from it shall have withdrawn and from its faith shall have detracted and its communion shall have rejected, let them hear by divine voice on the day of judgment: Depart from me, accursed, I know you not, go into eternal fire which has been prepared for the devil and his angels. Let therefore be damned in heaven and on earth, whatever through this catholic faith are damned, and let be accepted in heaven and on earth, whatever through this faith are accepted, our Lord Jesus Christ reigning, to whom with the Father and the Holy Spirit is glory unto ages of ages.","Qui umquam hanc fidem sanctam depravare, corrumpere, mutare temptaverit aut ab eadem fide vel communione catholica, quam nuper sumus deo miserante adepti, se separare vel dissociare voluerit, sit deo et universo mundo crimine infidelitatis in aeternum obnoxius. Floreat autem sancta ecclesia catholica per omnem mundum pacatissime et emineat doctrina sanctitate et potestate. Si qui intra eam fuerint communicaverintque, hi audiant ad dexteram patris positi: Venite, benedicti patris mei, percipite regnum, quod vobis paratum est ab origine mundi. Si qui autem ab ea recesserint eiusque detraxerint fidei et communionem respuerint, hi audiant ore divino in die iudicii: Discedite a me, maledicti, nescio vos, ite in ignem aeternum, qui paratus est diabolo et angelis eius. Sint ergo damnata in caelo et in terra, quaecumque per hanc catholicam fidem damnantur, et sint accepta in caelo et in terra, quaecumque per hanc fidem accipiuntur, regnante domino nostro Iesu Christo, cui cum patre et spiritu sancto est gloria in saecula saeculorum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p58","Incipit Fides a Sancto Niceno Concilio Edita.","We believe in one God the Father almighty, of all things visible and invisible the creator, and in one Lord Jesus Christ the Son of God from the Father born only-begotten, that is from the substance of the Father, God from God, light from light, true God from true God, born not made, homoousion to the Father, that is of the same with the Father substance, through whom all things were made, which in the heavens and which in the earth, who for us and for our salvation descended and was incarnate, suffered and rose again on the third day, ascended into heaven, from there he is to come to judge the living and the dead, and in the Holy Spirit. Those moreover who say, there was when he was not, and before he was born he was not, and that from non-existing things he was made or from another substance or subsistence they say him to be or convertible or changeable the Son of God, the catholic and apostolic church anathematizes.","Credimus in unum deum patrem omnipotentem omnium visibilium et invisibilium conditorem et in unum dominum Iesum Christum filium dei de patre natum unigenitum, hoc est de substantia patris, deum ex deo, lumen ex lumine, deum verum ex deo vero, natum non factum, homousion patri, hoc est eiusdem cum patre substantiae, per quem omnia facta sunt, quae in caelis et quae in terris, qui propter nos et propter nostram salutem descendit et incarnatus est, passus est et resurrexit tertia die, ascendit in caelos, inde venturus est iudicare vivos et mortuos, et in spiritum sanctum. Eos autem, qui dicunt, erat, quando non erat, et antequam nasceretur, non erat, et quia ex nullis exstantibus factus est aut ex alia substantia vel subsistentia dicunt esse aut convertibilem vel mutabilem filium dei, anathematizat catholica et apostolica ecclesia."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p59","Item Sancta Fides, Quam Exposuerunt CL Patres in Concilio Constantinopolitano.","We believe in one God the Father almighty, maker of heaven and earth, of all things visible and invisible the creator, and in one Lord Jesus Christ the Son of God only-begotten, from the Father born before all ages, God from God, light from light, true God from true God, born not made, homoousion to the Father, that is of the same with the Father substance, through whom all things were made, which in the heavens and which in the earth are, who for our salvation descended and was incarnate of the Holy Spirit and Mary the virgin, man was made, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was buried, on the third day rose again, ascended into heaven, sits at the right hand of the Father, again to come in glory to judge the living and the dead, of whose kingdom there shall be no end, and in the Holy Spirit the Lord and life-giver from the Father proceeding, with the Father and the Son to be adored and to be glorified, who spoke through the prophets, one catholic and apostolic church. We confess one baptism into remission of sins, we look for the resurrection of the dead, the life of the future age. Amen.","Credimus in unum deum patrem omnipotentem factorem caeli et terrae, visibilium omnium et invisibilium conditorem et in unum Iesum Christum filium dei unigenitum, ex patre natum ante omnia saecula, deum ex deo, lumen ex lumine, deum verum ex deo vero, natum non factum, homousion patri, hoc est, eiusdem cum patre substantiae, per quem omnia facta sunt, quae in caelis et quae in terris sunt, qui propter nostram salutem descendit et incarnatus est de spiritu sancto et Maria virgine, homo factus passus est sub Pontio Pilato, sepultus tertia die resurrexit, ascendit in caelos, sedet ad dexteram patris, iterum venturus in gloria iudicare vivos et mortuos, cuius regni non erit finis, et in spiritum sanctum dominum et vivificatorem ex patre procedentem cum patre et filio adorandum et glorificandum, qui locutus est per prophetas, unam catholicam atque apostolicam ecclesiam. Confitemur unum baptisma in remissionem peccatorum, exspectamus resurrectionem mortuorum, vitam futuri saeculi. Amen."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p60","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","It had sufficed indeed for the most full acknowledgment and confirmation of piety this most cautious salutary symbol of divine grace. For concerning the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit it teaches perfect doctrine and the Lord's incarnation to those faithfully receiving it manifests. But since those who the preaching of truth to destroy strive, certain novelties of their own heresy bring forth, some indeed the mystery for us wrought of the divine dispensation dare to corrupt and that voice of the virgin birth made to the virgin deny, others a mixture and confusion introducing and one to be the nature of flesh and of divinity insensibly composing, passible of the only-begotten the divine nature with such confession prodigiously divulge, therefore every against the truth to be opposed from them machine wishing to exclude, the holy and great universal synod the ancient preaching immovable teaching, established chiefly that the faith of the three hundred and eighteen holy fathers uncontaminated remain. And on account of those who to the Holy Spirit opposed, of the one hundred and fifty fathers a little later time in the city of Constantinople convening concerning the substance of the Holy Spirit handed down doctrine confirms, which also to all they made known, not that in the preceding something was lacking adding, but concerning the Holy Spirit of the same understanding, against those who the domination of his deity strive to take away by the testimonies of the Scriptures more fully manifesting. On account of those indeed who the mystery of the dispensation try to corrupt and a mere man to be who of the holy virgin was born impudently divulge, of the most blessed Cyril of the Alexandrian church priest the synodical epistles both to Nestorius and to the others through the East suitable and to himself consenting it receives for the confutation indeed of Nestorian madness, for the interpretation truly of those who with religious zeal of the salutary symbol the understanding seize, by which also the letter of the holy and most blessed of the first see the archbishop Leo to Flavian written of holy record the archbishop for destroying the malice of Eutyches, which to the confession of great Peter agrees and a certain common page existing against those who rightly do not glorify, for the confirmation of the catholic religion evidently it subjoined. For those who into two sons the mystery of the Lord's dispensation to split strive it execrates, and those who passible the divinity of the only-begotten Son of God dare to assert from the council of priests it repels, and those who in the two natures of Christ a mixture or confusion argue it opposes, and who of a heavenly or of any other substance to exist the form of a servant, which for us he assumed, in their madness assert, far it casts out, and those who two indeed before the union natures of the Lord rave, one after the union feign, anathema it makes. Consenting therefore to the holy fathers one and the same Son to confess our Lord Jesus Christ with consonant voice equally we are taught, perfect the same in humanity, true God and true man the same from rational soul and body, according to divinity of one with the Father nature, according to humanity the same of one nature with us, through all things like to us without sin, before ages indeed from the Father born according to divinity, in the last days indeed the same on account of us and on account of our salvation from Mary the virgin the Mother of God according to humanity one and the same Christ the Son the Lord only-begotten in two natures inconfusedly, immutably, indivisibly, inseparably knowing, in nothing of the natures the differences on account of the union to be destroyed, rather the property of each nature being saved and into one person and one state concurring, not into two persons to be divided or to be separated, but one and the same Son only-begotten true God Lord Jesus Christ, just as from the beginning the prophets concerning him, and he himself taught us, and the symbol of the fathers handed down to us.","Suffecerat quidem ad plenissimam pietatis agnitionem et confirmationem cautissimum hoc salutare divinae gratiae symbolum. De patre enim et filio et spiritu sancto doctrinam perfectam edocet et incarnationem dominicam fideliter suscipientibus manifestat. Sed quoniam hi, qui praedicationem veritatis destruere nituntur, quasdam propriae hereseos novitates partiunt, quidam enim mysterium pro nobis actum divinae dispensationis audent corrumpere et vocem illam virginei partus factam ad virginem denegant, alii temperamentum confusionemque inducentes et unam esse naturam carnis et deitatis insensate componentes, passibilem unigeniti divinam naturam tali confessione prodigiose divulgant, idcirco omnem adversus veritatem opponendam ab ipsis machinationem volens excludere sancta et magna universalis synodus antiquam praedicationem immobilem docens, statuit praecipue trecentorum decem et octo sanctorum patrum fidem incontaminatam manere. Et propter eos, qui spiritui sancto adversabantur, CL patrum paulo posteriori tempore in urbe Constantinopolitana convenientium de substantia spiritus sancti traditam doctrinam corroborat, quam etiam omnibus insinuaverunt, non quod in praecedentibus aliquid deesset adicientes, sed de spiritu sancto eorundem intellectus adversus eos, qui deitatis dominationem nituntur adimere scripturarum testimoniis plenius manifestantes. Propter eos sane, qui dispensationis mysterium temptant corrumpere et purum hominem esse, qui ex sancta virgine natus est, impudenter divulgant, beatissimi quondam Cyrilli Alexandrinae ecclesiae sacerdotis synodicas epistolas tam ad Nestorium quam ad ceteros per orientem congruas et sibi consentientes suscepit ad confutationem quidem Nestorianae amentiae et ad interpretationem eorum, qui religioso zelo salutaris symboli capiunt intellectum, quibus et epistolam sancti ac beatissimi primae sedis archiepiscopi Leonis ad Flavianum scriptam sanctae recordationis archiepiscopum ad perimendam Euticetis malignitatem, quaeque magni Petri confessione concordat et communem quandam paginam exsistentem contra eos, qui recte non glorificant ad confirmationem catholicae religionis evidenter subiunxit. Nam eos, qui in duos filios dispensationis dominicae mysterium scindere moliuntur, exsecratur et eos, qui passibilem divinitatem unigeniti filii dei audent asserere, de concilio sacerdotum repellit, et eos, qui in duabus naturis Christi temperamentum vel confusionem argumentantur, adversatur, et qui caelestem aut alterius cuiusque substantiae exsistere formam servi, quam pro nobis assumpsit, insaniendo asserunt, procul abicit, et eos, qui duas quidem ante adunationem naturas domini delirant, unam vero post adunationem confingunt, anathema facit. Consentientes igitur sanctis patribus unum eundemque filium confiteri dominum nostrum Iesum Christum consona voce pariter edocemur, perfectum eundem in humanitate, deum verum et hominem verum eundem ex anima rationali et corpore, secundum divinitatem unius cum patre naturae, secundum humanitatem eundem unius naturae nobiscum, per omnia similem nobis absque peccato, ante saecula quidem ex patre natum secundum divinitatem, in novissimis vero diebus eundem propter nos et propter nostram salutem ex Maria virgine dei genetrice secundum humanitatem unum eundemque Christum filium dominum unigenitum in duabus naturis inconfuse, immutabiliter, indivise, inseparabiliter cognoscendo, in nullo naturarum differentias propter unitatem perimendas, magis autem salva utriusque naturae proprietate et in una coeunte persona unoque statu concurrente, non in duabus personis partiendum vel dividendum, sed unum eundemque filium unigenitum deum verum dominum Iesum Christum, sicut ab exordio prophetae de eo, et ipse nos erudivit, et patrum nobis tradidit symbolum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p61","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","These things therefore with all subtlety and diligence by us having been ordered, the holy and universal synod established another faith to none to be allowed to bring forth and to write or to publish or to separate or to teach otherwise. Who moreover dare to set forth another faith or to bring forth or to teach or to hand down another symbol to those wishing to be converted to the knowledge of the truth from Gentiles or from Jews or from heretics any, if indeed bishops or clerics they shall have been, strangers to be bishops from the episcopate and clerics from the clergy we command; if truly monks or laymen they shall have been, with anathema let them be struck.","His itaque cum omni subtilitate et diligentia a nobis ordinatis, statuit sancta et universalis synodus aliam fidem nulli licere proferre et scribere aut edere aut separare aut docere aliter. Qui autem audent exponere aliam fidem aut proferre aut docere aut tradere alium symbolum volentibus converti ad scientiam veritatis ex gentibus vel Iudaeis vel hereticis quibuscumque, si quidem episcopi aut clerici fuerint, alienos esse episcopos ab episcopatu et clericos a clero praecipimus, si vero monachi aut laici fuerint, anathemate feriantur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p62","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Anastasius, in the name of Christ bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Murila, in the name of Christ bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Vuiliscus, in the name of Christ bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Sumnila, in the name of Christ of the city of Veseo bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Gardingus, in the name of Christ of the city of Tui bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Beccila, in the name of Christ of the city of Lugo bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Arbitrus, in the name of Christ of the city of Portugal bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Fruisclus, in the name of Christ of the city of Tortosa bishop, anathematizing the heresy of the Arian dogma above damned, this holy catholic faith, which in the catholic church coming I believed, with my hand from all my heart have subscribed. Similarly also the rest of the presbyters and deacons from the Arian heresy converted subscribed.","Anastasius in Christi nomine episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Murila in Christi nomine episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis, superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Vuiliscus in Christi nomine episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Sumnila in Christi nomine civitatis Vesensis episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Gardingus in Christi nomine civitatis Tudensis episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Beccila in Christi nomine civitatis Lucensis episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Arbitrus in Christi nomine civitatis Portucalensis episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Fruisclus in Christi nomine civitatis Dertosanae episcopus anathematizans heresim Arriani dogmatis superius damnatam fidem hanc sanctam catholicam, quam in ecclesia catholica veniens credidi, manu mea de toto corde subscripsi. Similiter et reliqui presbyteri et diacones ex heresi Arriana conversi subscripserunt."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p63","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","The sign of Gussinus, illustrious man and noble. Fonsa, illustrious man, anathematizing subscribed. Afrila, illustrious man, anathematizing subscribed. Abila, illustrious man, anathematizing subscribed. Elavi, illustrious man, anathematizing subscribed. Similarly also all the elders of the Goths subscribed.","Signum Gussini viri illustris proceris. Fonsa vir illuster anathematizans subscripsi. Afrila vir illuster anathematizans subscripsi. Abila vir illuster anathematizans subscripsi. Elavi vir illuster anathematizans subscripsi. Similiter et omnes seniores Gothorum subscripserunt."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p64","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","After the confession therefore and subscription of all the bishops and of all the elders of the Gothic nation, the most glorious lord our king Recared for restoring together and confirming the customs of ecclesiastical discipline thus addressed the priests of God, saying:","Post confessionem igitur et subscriptionem omnium episcoporum et totius gentis Gothicae seniorum gloriosissimus domnus noster Recaredus rex pro reparandis simul et confirmandis disciplinae ecclesiasticae moribus dei sacerdotes taliter adfectus est dicens:"],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p65","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Royal care even to that degree ought to be extended and directed, to the extent that full it may have been established of age and of knowledge to take the reason. For just as in human things more gloriously excels the royal power, so also for looking to the advantage of fellow-provincial greater ought to be both the providence. And now, most blessed priests, not in those things only do we diffuse our skill, for which peoples under our governance, but also in those which by your sanctity to the ecclesiastical rules are to be added, this on behalf of the reverence and firmness of the holy faith propose, which concerning bringing forth the symbol our to God teaching serenity decreed. Moreover concerning prohibiting the insolent customs, by my to you consenting clemency with sentences terminated stricter and with firm discipline, those things which are not to be done prohibit, and placed most peacefully let them be governed and live.","Regia cura usque in eum modum protendi debet et dirigi, quoadusque plenam constiterit aetatis et scientiae capere rationem. Nam sicut in rebus humanis gloriosius eminet potestas regia, ita et prospiciendae commoditati comprovincialium maior debet esse et providentia. Ac nunc, beatissimi sacerdotes, non in eis tantummodo rebus diffundimus sollertiam nostram, quibus populi sub nostro regimine, sed etiam in his quae per vestram sanctitatem regulis ecclesiasticis adicienda sunt, hoc pro fidei sanctae reverentia et firmitate proponite, quod de proferendo symbolo nostra deo docente decrevit serenitas. De cetero autem prohibendis insolentium moribus mea vobis consentiente clementia sententiis terminatis districtioribus et firma disciplina, quae facienda non sunt, prohibete et positi pacatissime gubermentur et vivant."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p66","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","But also in the help of Christ we extend ourselves to those things which are heavenly to think and which the peoples faithful may make, we strive not to be ignorant. Moreover if with all strength it must be striven human customs to set a limit and the rage of insolent by royal power to restrain, if to quiet and to peace to be propagated help we ought to expend, much more is diligence to be applied to desire and to think divine things. To gape at sublime things and from error having been withdrawn to the peoples the truth of serene light to show. For thus acts he who by manifold good himself by God to be rewarded trusts, for thus hears he who upon that which to him is committed increases, while to him it is said: Whatever you shall have expended beyond, I, when I shall have returned, will give back to you.","sed etiam in adiutorio Christi extendimus nos ad ea, quae sunt caelestia cogitare et quae populos fideles efficiant, satagimus non nescire. Ceterum si totis nitendum est viribus humanis moribus modum ponere et insolentium rabiem regia potestate refrenare, si quieti et paci propagandae opem debemus impendere, multo magis est adhibenda sollicitudo desiderare et cogitare divina. Inhiare sublimia et ab errore retractis populis veritatem eis serenae lucis ostendere, sic enim agit, qui multiplici bono se a deo remunerari confidit, sic enim audit, qui super id, quod ei committitur, auget, dum illi dicitur: Quicquid supererogaveris, ego, cum rediero, reddam tibi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p67","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Therefore because already of our faith and confession the form with full series your blessedness has recited together and the faith and confession of our priests and chief men to your sanctity has been made plain, this still necessary for the firmness of the catholic faith by our to God suppliant authority has decreed to establish, that for strengthening the new conversion of our nation all the churches of the Spains and of Gaul this rule should guard, that at every time of sacrifice before the communion of the body of Christ and of the blood according to the custom of the eastern parts with unanimous voice and clear the most sacred symbol of the faith they should recite, that first the peoples, what belief they hold, may profess and thus with hearts by faith purified to receive the body and blood of Christ they may present themselves. For while this constitution shall have been perpetually preserved in the church of God, both the belief of the faithful is strengthened and the perfidy of the unfaithful being confuted to that which having been often repeated it recognizes most easily is inclined, nor will anyone now from ignorance of the faith excuse himself from fault, when by the mouth of all he knows what the catholic church holds and believes.","Ergo quia iam fidei nostrae et confessionis formam plena serie vestra beatitudo recensuit simul et sacerdotum nostrorumque procerum fides atque confessio sanctitati vestrae perpatuit, hoc adhuc necessarium pro firmitate catholicae fidei nostra deo supplex instituere decrevit auctoritas, ut propter roborandam gentis nostrae novellam conversionem omnes Spaniarum et Galliae ecclesiae hanc regulam servent, omni sacrificii tempore ante communicationem corporis Christi vel sanguinis iuxta orientalium partium morem unanimiter clara voce sacratissimum fidei recenseant symbolum, ut primum populi, quam credulitatem teneant, fateantur et sic corda fide purificata ad Christi corpus et sanguinem percipiendum exhibeant. Dum enim constitutio haec fuerit perenniter conservata in dei ecclesia et fidelium ex solido corroboratur credulitas et perfidia infidelium confutata ad id, quod repetitum saepius recognoscit, facillime inclinatur nec se quisquam iam de ignorantia fidei excusabit a culpa, quando universorum ore cognoscit, quid catholica teneat et credat ecclesia."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p68","Item Tractatus Chalcedonensis Concilii.","Therefore all chapters, which are to be done, with immovable constitution strengthen.","Omnibus ergo capitulis, quae fieri debent, immobili constitutione firmate."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p69","Incipiunt Capitula, Quae in Dei Nomine Sancta Synodus in Toletana Urbe Constitui","VI. That a slave of the church by a bishop manumitted from the patronage of the church never depart, and that the freedmen of others by a bishop be defended.","VI. Ut servus ecclesiae ab episcopo manumissus a patrocinio ecclesiae numquam recedat, et ut liberti aliorum ab episcopo defendantur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p70","VII. That at the table of the bishop the divine Scriptures be read.","XII. Of those who seek penance: if it is a man, first let him be tonsured; if a woman, first let her change the habit.",""],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p71","XII. De his, qui poenitentiam poscunt, si vir est, prius tondatur, si femina pri","XXII. That the bodies of the religious only with psalmody be led forth, and that on the natal days of the saints dances be prohibited.","XXII. Ut religiosorum corpora psallendo tantum deducantur et ut in sanctorum nataliciis ballimathiae prohibeantur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p72","Canon I","After the damnation of the Arian heresy and the exposition of the holy catholic faith, this holy council commanded, that, because by some either of heresy or of gentility by necessity through the Spanish churches the canonical order has been omitted, while both the license of transgressing abounded and the choice of discipline was denied, while every excess of heresy was proven by the patronage and the abundance of evil time, and far off was the strictness of discipline, but now with the peace of the church by mercy repaired, everything that the authority of the ancient canons prohibits, let it be with discipline reviving inhibited, and let everything be done which it commands. Let remain in their vigor the constitutions of all councils together and the synodical letters of the holy Roman prelates. Let no one thereafter for acquiring ecclesiastical honors against the canons aspire unworthy. Let nothing from this be done which the holy fathers, full of the Spirit of God, sanctioned ought not to be done, and who shall have presumed, by the severity of the prior canons let him be restrained.","Post damnationem heresis Arrianae et fidei sanctae catholicae expositionem hoc sanctum praecepit concilium, ut, quia a nonnullis vel heresis vel gentilitatis necessitate per Spaniarum ecclesias canonicus praetermissus est ordo, dum et licentia abundaret transgrediendi et disciplinae optio negaretur, dum omnis excessus heresis probaretur patrocinio et abundantia mali temporis, procul et districtio disciplinae, at nunc pace ecclesiae Christi misericordia reparata omne, quod priscorum canonum auctoritas prohibet, sit resurgente disciplina inhibitum, et agatur omne, quod praecepit. Permaneant in suo vigore conciliorum omnium constituta simul et synodicae sanctorum praesulum Romanorum epistolae. Nullus deinceps ad promerendos honores ecclesiasticos contra canonum aspiret indignus. Nihil ex hoc fiat, quod sancti patres spiritu dei pleni sanxerunt debere non fieri, et qui praesumpserit, severitate priorum canonum distringatur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p73","Canon II","For the reverence of the most holy faith and for strengthening the weak minds of men, by the counsel of the most pious and most glorious Recared the king, the synod established, that through all the churches of Spain and Gaul or Galicia according to the form of the eastern churches of the council of Constantinople, that is of the one hundred and fifty bishops, the symbol of faith be recited, and before the Lord's prayer be said, with clear voice be preached to the people, that both the true faith may be manifest and have testimony, and to the body and blood of Christ to be prelibated the breasts of the people by faith purified may approach.","Pro reverentia sanctissimae fidei et propter corroborandas hominum invalidas mentes consulto piissimi et gloriosissimi Recaredi regis constituit synodus, ut per omnes ecclesias Spaniae et Galliae vel Galliciae secundum formam orientalium ecclesiarum concilii Constantinopolitani, hoc est centum quinquaginta episcoporum, symbolum fidei recitetur, et priusquam dominica dicatur oratio, voce clara praedicetur populo, quo et fides vera manifesta sit et testimonium habeat et ad Christi corpus et sanguinem praelibandum pectora populorum fide purificata accedant."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p74","Canon III","This holy synod to no bishop does license grant the property of the church to alienate, since even by the more ancient canons this is prohibited. If indeed anything which the utility of the church not burden, for the support of monks or of churches to his own parish belonging they shall have given, let it remain firm. To the necessity of strangers or of clerics and of the needy, the right of the church being saved, they are permitted for the time to supply what they shall have been able.","Haec sancta synodus nulli episcoporum licentiam tribuit res alienare ecclesiae, quoniam et antiquioribus canonibus hoc prohibetur. Si quid vero, quod utilitatem non gravet ecclesiae, pro suffragio monachorum vel ecclesiis ad suam parrochiam pertinentium dederint, firmum maneat. Peregrinorum vel clericorum et egenorum necessitati salvo iure ecclesiae praestare permittuntur pro tempore, quae potuerint."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p75","Canon IIII","If a bishop one of his parish churches into a monastery to consecrate shall have willed, that in it of monks regularly a congregation may live, let him have the license of doing this with the consent of his council. He also, if from the goods of the church for their sustenance anything which detriment to the church may not cause, to the same place he shall have donated, let it be stable. For a good thing the holy council, establishing, gives consent.","Si episcopus unam de parrochitanis ecclesiis suis monasterium dicare voluerit, ut in ea monachorum regulariter congregatio vivat, hoc de consensu concilii sui habeat licentiam faciendi. Qui etiam, si de rebus ecclesiae pro eorum substantia aliquid, quo detrimentum ecclesiae non exhibeat, eidem loco donaverit, sit stabile. Rei enim bonae statuendum sanctum concilium dat consensum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p76","Canon V","It has been discovered by the holy council that bishops, presbyters, and deacons coming from the heresy with carnal desire still to their wives are joined. Lest therefore from now on it be done, this is commanded, which also in the prior canons is contained, that it not be lawful for them to live in libidinous society, but remaining between them the conjugal faith, let them have common utility and not under one roof remain, or certainly if virtue supports, into another house his wife let him cause to live, that chastity before God and before men may have a good testimony. If any indeed after this convention obscenely with his wife shall have chosen to live, as neglected thus let him be held. Those who always under the ecclesiastical canon have lain, if against the commands of the ancients in their cells with women, which the suspicion of infamy can generate, they shall have had consortium, let them canonically indeed be constrained, the women indeed by the bishops let them be sold, the price itself to the poor be distributed.","Compertum est a sancto concilio episcopos, presbyteros et diaconos venientes ex heresi carnali adhuc desiderio uxoribus copulari. Ne ergo de cetero fiat, hoc praecipitur, quod et prioribus canonibus continetur, ut non liceat eis vivere libidinosa societate, sed manente inter eos fide coniugali communem utilitatem habeant et non sub uno conclavi maneant, vel certe si suffragatur virtus in aliam domum suam uxorem faciat habitare, ut castitas apud deum et apud homines habeat testimonium bonum. Si qui vero post hanc conventionem obscene cum uxore elegerit vivere, ut neglecto ita habeatur. Qui vero semper sub canone ecclesiastico iacuerunt, si contra veterum imperata in suis cellulis mulierum, quae infamiae suspicionem possunt generare, consortium habuerint, illi canonice quidem distringantur, mulieres vero ab episcopis venundatae, pretium ipsum pauperibus erogetur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p77","Canon VI","Concerning freedmen moreover this the holy synod commanded, that, if any presbyters or deacons by bishops have been made, according to the manner which the ancient canons give license, let them be free, and yet from the patronage of the church both themselves and those procreated from them not depart. From others also to liberty given over and to churches commended, by the patronage of the bishop let them be gathered, and that they be given to no one by the prince, this let the bishop request.","De libertis autem hoc praecepit sancta synodus, ut, si qui presbyteri vel diaconi ab episcopis facti sunt, secundum modum, quo canones antiqui dant licentiam, sint liberi, et tamen a patrocinio ecclesiae tam ipsi quam ab eis progeniti non recedant. Ab aliis quoque libertati traditi et ecclesiis commendati patrocinio episcopi colligantur, et ne cuiquam donentur a principe, hoc episcopus postulet."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p78","Canon VII","For the reverence of God and of the priests the whole synod established, that, because they are accustomed frequently to the table idle tales to interpose, in every priestly banquet the reading of the divine Scriptures be mingled. By this indeed the souls are edified unto good and unnecessary tales are prohibited.","Pro reverentia dei et sacerdotum id universa constituit synodus, ut, quia solent crebro mensis otiosae fabulae interponi, in omni sacerdotali convivio lectio scripturarum divinarum misceatur. Per hoc enim et animae aedificantur ad bonum et fabulae non necessariae prohibentur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p79","Canon VIII","The Lord Recared the king ordering and consenting, this the priestly council commanded, that clerics from the family of the fisc no one should dare from the prince donated to seek, but delivered let them the tribute of their head to the church of God, to which they are attached, as long as they live, according to rule administer.","Iubente autem atque consentiente domino Recaredo rege id praecepit sacerdotale concilium, ut clericos ex familia fisci nullus audeat a principe donatos expetere, sed traditos capitis sui tributum ecclesiae dei, cui sunt alligati, usque dum vivunt, regulariter administrent."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p80","Canon VIIII","By the decree of this council it is established, that the churches which were in the Arian heresy, now indeed are catholic, to those bishops with their goods pertain, to whom the parishes themselves, in which the churches themselves are founded, are seen to pertain.","Decreto huius concilii hoc statuitur, ut ecclesiae, quae fuerunt in heresi Arriana, nunc autem sunt catholicae, ad eos episcopos cum suis rebus pertineant, ad quos parrochiae ipsae, in quibus ecclesiae ipsae fundatae sunt, pertinere videntur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p81","Canon X","For the counsel of chastity, which especially by the exhortation of the council ought to profit, the glorious lord our king Recared consenting, this holy council affirms, that widows, to whom it shall have pleased, let them hold chastity, and let no widow to entering marriages be compelled to come. But if, before they profess continence, to marry they shall have chosen, let them marry those whom by their own will they shall have willed to have as husbands. Let a similar condition also concerning virgins be held, nor outside the will of their parents or their own let them be compelled husbands to take. If anyone indeed the purpose of chastity of a widow or of a virgin shall have impeded, from holy communion and from the thresholds of the church let him be held a stranger.","Pro consulto castitatis, quod maxime hortamento concilii proficere debeat, annuente glorioso domino nostro Recaredo rege, hoc sanctum affirmat concilium, ut viduae, quibus placuerit, teneant castitatem et nulla vidua ad nuptias intrandas venire cogatur. Quod si, priusquam profiteantur continentiam, nubere elegerint, illis nubant, quos propria voluntate voluerint habere maritos. Similis condicio et de virginibus habeatur, nec extra voluntatem parentum vel suam cogantur maritos accipere. Si quis vero propositum castitatis viduae vel virginis impedierit, a sancta communione et a liminibus ecclesiae habeatur extraneus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p82","Canon XI","Because we have found through certain Spanish churches not according to the canon, but most foully for their sins men to do penance, and as often as it shall have pleased them to sin, so often by presbyters themselves to be reconciled they demand. And therefore for restraining so execrable a presumption, this by the holy council is ordered, that according to the form of the ancient canons penance be given, that is, first let him whom he repents of the deed, from communion suspended, cause among the rest of the penitents to the imposition of hands frequently to recur. The time of satisfaction having been fulfilled, just as the priestly consideration shall have approved, let him restore him to communion. Those indeed who to their own vices either within the time of penance or after reconciliation relapse, according to the severity of the prior canons let them be damned.","Quoniam comperimus per quasdam Spaniarum ecclesias non secundum canonem, sed foedissime pro suis peccatis homines agere poenitentiam, et quoties peccare libuerit, toties a presbyteris se reconciliari expostulent. Et ideo pro coercenda tam exsecrabili praesumptione, id a sancto concilio iubetur, ut secundum formam canonum antiquorum detur poenitentia, hoc est, ut prius eum, quem sui poenitet facti, a communione suspensum faciat inter reliquos poenitentes ad manus impositionem crebro recurrere. Expleto autem satisfactionis tempore, sicuti sacerdotalis contemplatio probaverit, eum communioni restituat. Hi vero, qui ad propria vitia vel infra poenitentiae tempus vel post reconciliationem relabuntur, secundum priorum canonum severitate damnentur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p83","Canon XII","Whoever by a bishop or presbyter sound or infirm penance seeks, this before all things let the bishop observe and the presbyter, that, if it is a man whether sound or infirm, first he tonsure him or into ashes and sackcloth the habit to change cause, and thus penance to him deliver. If indeed a woman shall have been, let her not receive penance, unless first she either be veiled or have changed the habit. For often to laics or women given slothfully penance to again to be lamented crimes after received penance they relapse.","Quicumque ab episcopo vel presbytero sanus vel infirmus poenitentiam postulat, id ante omnia episcopus observet et presbyter, ut, si vir est sive sanus sive infirmus, prius eum tondat aut in cinere et cilicio habitum mutare faciat et sic poenitentiam ei tradat. Si vero mulier fuerit, non accipiat poenitentiam, nisi prius aut velata fuerit aut mutaverit habitum. Saepius enim laicis vel feminis tribuendo desidiose poenitentiam ad lamentanda rursus facinora post acceptam poenitentiam relabuntur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p84","Canon XIII","Inveterate presumption even to illicit daring access has opened, so that clerics their fellow clerics, their pontiff having been left, to public judgments drag. Therefore we establish that this from now on not be presumed. If anyone shall have presumed to do this, let him be convened and both his case lose and from communion be made a stranger.","Inolita praesumptio usque adeo illicitis ausibus aditum patefecit, ut clerici conclericos suos relicto pontifice suo ad iudicia publica pertrahant. Proinde statuimus, ut hoc de cetero non praesumatur. Si quis hoc praesumpserit facere, conventus et causam perdat et a communione efficiatur extraneus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p85","Canon XIIII","Our to these canons to be inserted commanded, that it not be lawful for Jews to have Christian wives or concubines nor a Christian slave for their own uses to purchase, but also the sons who from such marriage have been born, to be assumed to baptism. Let no public offices to them be entrusted, through which to them an occasion be granted to inflict punishment on Christians. If any indeed Christians by them by the Jewish rite have been defiled or even circumcised, let them, the price not having been returned, to liberty and Christian religion return.","Noster hoc canonibus inserendum praecepit, ut Iudaeis non liceat christianas habere uxores vel concubinas neque mancipium christianum in usus proprios comparare, sed et filii, qui ex tali coniugio nati sunt, assumendos esse ad baptismum. Nulla officia publica eis iniungantur, per quae eis occasio tribuatur poenam christianis inferre. Si qui vero christiani ab eis iudaismo ritu sunt maculati vel etiam circumcisi, non reddito pretio ad libertatem et religionem redeant christianam."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p86","Canon XV","If any from the fiscal slaves perhaps churches shall have built and them from their poverty shall have dowered, let this the bishop procure by his prayer to be confirmed by authority.","Si qui ex servis fiscalibus fortasse ecclesias construxerint easque de sua paupertate dotaverint, hoc procuret episcopus prece sua auctoritate confirmari."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p87","Canon XVI","Because nearly through all Spain and Gaul the sacrilege of idolatry has grown strong, this with the consent of the most glorious prince the holy synod ordered, that every priest in his place together with the judge of the territory the remembered sacrilege studiously search out and having been found to destroy not delay. All indeed who to such error run together, without distinction, with what punishment they shall have been able, let them coerce. But if they shall have neglected, let them know that both the peril of excommunication are about to undergo. If any indeed masters this evil from their possession to extirpate shall have neglected or to their family to prohibit shall have been unwilling, by the bishop even themselves from communion let them be driven.","Quoniam pene per omnem Spaniam sive Galliam idolatriae sacrilegium inolevit, hoc cum consensu gloriosissimi principis sancta synodus ordinavit, ut omnis sacerdos in loco suo una cum iudice territorii sacrilegium memoratum studiose perquirat et exterminari inventum non differat. Omnes vero, qui ad talem errorem concurrunt, sine discrimine, qua potuerint animadversione, coerceant. Quod si neglexerint, sciant se utrique excommunicationis periculum esse subituros. Si qui vero domini exstirpare hoc malum de possessione sua neglexerint vel familiae prohibere noluerint, ab episcopo et ipsi a communione pellantur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p88","Canon XVII","While many complaints to the ears of the holy council were being brought, among other things of such great cruelty a work was reported, as the ears of the sitting priests are not able to endure, that in certain parts of Spain parents their own sons kill, eager for fornication, of piety alien. To whom if it is wearisome to have children more numerous, first themselves they ought to castigate from fornication. For while for the sake of producing offspring they obtain marriages, by parricide and fornication they are held liable, who by killing their own sons teach themselves not for sons but for lust wives to have taken. Therefore so great a crime to the knowledge of the most glorious lord our king Recared was brought, whose glory deigned to the judges of those parts to command, that to be removed so great a crime diligently with the priest they procure and with severity observed prohibit. Therefore also the priests of those same places, in which the enormity of this crime is perpetrated, the holy synod by commanding convenes, that the same crime with the judge more curiously they search out and without capital vengeance with stricter discipline prohibit.","Dum multae querelae ad aures sancti concilii deferrentur, inter cetera tantae crudelitatis est opus nuntiatum, quantum consedentium aures sacerdotum non possunt sustinere, ut in quibusdam Spaniae partibus filios suos parentes interimant fornicatione avidi, pietatis alieni. Quibus si taedium est filios numerosius agere, prius se ipsos debent castigare a fornicatione. Nam dum causa propagandae prolis sortiantur coniugia, parricidio et fornicatione tenentur obnoxii, qui filios necando proprios docent se non pro filiis, sed pro libidine uxores duxisse. Proinde tantum nefas ad cognitionem gloriosissimi domini nostri Recaredi regis perlatum est, cuius gloria dignata est iudicibus earundem partium imperare, ut amovendum tantum facinus diligenter cum sacerdote procurent et habita severitate prohibeant. Ergo et sacerdotes locorum eorundem, in quibus sceleris huius immanitas peragitur, sancta synodus praecipiendo convenit, ut idem scelus cum iudice curiosius quaerant et sine capitali vindicta acriori disciplina prohibeant."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p89","Canon XVIII","This holy and universal synod commands, the authority of the prior canons standing, which twice in a year commanded councils to be gathered, the consulted length of the journey and the poverty of the churches of Spain being considered, once in a year in the place which the metropolitan shall have chosen, let the bishops gather. The judges indeed of the places or the actors of the fiscal patrimonies by the decree of our lord together with the priestly council in autumn time on the day of the Kalends of November into one let them convene, that they may learn how piously and justly with the peoples they ought to act, lest in angaries or in superfluous works either a private person they burden or the fiscal they oppress. Let them be indeed observers the bishops according to the royal admonition, how the judges with the peoples act, that them having been forewarned they may correct or their insolence to the ears of the princes make known. But if them having been corrected to amend they shall not have been able, both from the church and from communion let them suspend. And by the priest and the elders let it be deliberated, what through the provinces in their own detriment they ought to provide the judges, if to the council they shall not have come. The council indeed not be dissolved, unless they shall have first chosen a place, to which at the following time again to the council they may come, that now not necessary may have the metropolitan bishop for gathering a council letters to send, if in the prior council the time is announced to all and the place.","Praecipit haec sancta et universalis synodus, ut stante priorum auctoritate canonum, quae bis in anno praecepit congregari concilia, consulta itineris longitudine et paupertate ecclesiarum Spaniae, semel in anno in loco, quem metropolitanus elegerit, episcopi congregentur. Iudices vero locorum vel actores fiscalium patrimoniorum ex decreto domini nostri simul cum sacerdotum concilio autumnali tempore die Kal. Novembr. in unum conveniant, ut discant, quam pie et iuste cum populis agere debeant, ne in angariis aut in operationibus superfluis sive privatum onerent sive fiscalem gravent. Sint etenim perspectores episcopi secundum regiam monitionem, qualiter iudices cum populis agant, ut ipsos praemonitos corrigant aut insolentias eorum auribus principum innotescant. Quod si correptos emendare nequiverint, et ab ecclesia et a communione suspendant. A sacerdote vero et senioribus deliberetur, quid per provincias in suo detrimento praestare debeant iudices, si ad concilium non venerint. Concilium autem non solvatur, nisi locum prius elegerint, quo succedenti tempore iterum ad concilium veniatur, ut iam non necesse habeat metropolitanus episcopus pro congregando concilio litteras destinare, si in priori concilio tempus omnibus denuntiatur et locus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p90","Canon XVIIII","If indeed against all authority churches which they shall have built they demand to be consecrated, that the dowry which to the same church they have contributed they may think to the ordinance of the bishop not to pertain, which has been done thus in the past, let it be corrected and in the future, lest it be done, is prohibited. But all things according to the ancient constitution to the bishop's ordinance and power pertain.","Si quidem contra omnem auctoritatem ecclesias, quas aedificaverint, postulant consecrari, ut dotem, quam eidem ecclesiae contulerint, censeant ad episcopi ordinationem non pertinere, quod factum est taliter in praeterito, corrigatur et in futuro, ne fiat, prohibetur. Sed omnia secundum constitutionem antiquam ad episcopi ordinationem et potestatem pertineant."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p91","Canon XX","Because we have known bishops through their parishes not as priests but cruelly to rage, and while it is written: Be a form to the flock not as dominating over the clergy, and the exactions of their diocese or harms they inflict. Therefore we decree, except that which the constitutions of the ancients from the parishes to have they order bishops, that other things to them which hitherto have been presumed be denied, that is neither in angaries presbyters or deacons nor in any indictions let them fatigue, lest we seem in the church of God exactors rather than of God pontiffs to be named. Those indeed clerics both local and diocesan, who themselves by the bishop to be burdened shall have known, their complaints to the metropolitan to bring not delay, that the metropolitan not delay such presumptions to coerce.","Quia cognovimus episcopos per parrochias suas non sacerdotaliter, sed crudeliter desaevire, et dum scriptum sit: Forma estote gregi non ut dominantes in clero, exactionesque diocesis suae vel damna infligant. Ideoque censemus excepto, quod veterum constitutiones a parrochiis habere iubent episcopos, ut alia illis, quae hucusque praesumpta sunt, denegentur, hoc est neque in angariis presbyteris aut diaconibus neque in aliquibus fatigent indictionibus, ne videamur in ecclesia dei exactores potius quam dei pontifices nominari. Hi vero clerici tam locales, quam diocesani, qui se ab episcopo gravare cognoverint, querelas suas ad metropolitanum deferre non differant, ut metropolitanus non moretur eiusmodi praesumptiones coercere."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p92","Canon XXI","The slaves of the churches and of the bishops or of all clerics by the judges or public actors in various angaries to be fatigued we grieve. For which thing the whole council from the piety of the most glorious lord sought, that such from now on daring he may inhibit, but the slaves of the above-written offices in their own uses or of the church let them labor. If any indeed of the judges or of the actors a cleric or a slave of a cleric or of the church in public or private businesses to occupy shall have willed, from ecclesiastical communion, which impediment he makes, let him be made a stranger.","Ecclesiarum servos et episcoporum vel omnium clericorum a iudicibus vel actoribus publicis in diversis angariis fatigari dolemus. Propter quod omne concilium a pietate gloriosissimi domini nostri poposcit, ut tales deinceps ausus inhibeat, sed servi suprascriptorum officiorum in eorum usibus vel ecclesiae laborent. Si qui vero iudicum aut actorum clericum aut servum clerici vel ecclesiae in publicis ac privatis negotiis occupare voluerit, a communione ecclesiastica, cui impedimentum facit, efficiatur extraneus."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p93","Canon XXII","Who by divine calling from this life depart, with psalms only and the voices of those singing psalms ought to the sepulchers to be carried. For the lamentation of the funeral, which vulgarly for the dead to be sung is wont, or to beat themselves or their neighbors or families to give up altogether we prohibit. Let it suffice indeed, that in the hope of the resurrection of the Christians the service of divine songs is imparted to the bodies. For the holy apostle forbids us the dead to mourn, saying: Concerning those sleeping, I do not wish you to be saddened, as also others who hope have not. And the Lord did not weep for Lazarus dead, but to the hardships of this life he wept for him to be raised up. If indeed this the bishop can, let him not delay to prohibit all Christians. For the religious indeed altogether otherwise to be done we decree. For thus the bodies of the dead of Christians through all the world ought to be buried.","Qui divina vocatione ab hac vita recedunt, cum psalmis tantummodo et psallentium vocibus debere ad sepulchra deferri. Nam funeris precamen, quod vulgo defunctis cantari solet vel pectoribus se aut proximos aut familias cedere omnino prohibemus. Sufficiat autem, quod in spe resurrectionis christianorum corporibus famulatus divinorum impenditur canticorum. Prohibet enim nos apostolus sanctus lugere defunctos dicens: De dormientibus autem nolo vos contristari, sicut et ceteri, qui spem non habent. Et dominus non flevit Lazarum mortuum, sed ad huius vitae aerumnas ploravit resuscitandum. Si enim potest hoc episcopus, omnes christianos prohibere agere non moretur. Religiosis tamen omnino aliter fieri non debere censemus. Sic enim christianorum per omnem mundum humari oportet corpora defunctorum."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p94","Canon XXIII","An irreligious custom is that which the vulgus through the solemnities of the saints to do is wont. Peoples, who ought divine offices to attend, to turpid dances they are intent, songs not only evil singing but even with the offices of the religious clamoring. This therefore that from all Spain be driven away, to the care of the priests and the judges by the holy council is committed.","Irreligiosa consuetudo est, quam vulgus per sanctorum solemnitates agere consuevit. Populi, qui debent officia divina attendere, saltationibus turpibus invigilant, cantica non solum mala canentes, sed et religiosorum officiis perstrepentes. Hoc etenim, ut ab omni Spania depellatur, sacerdotum et iudicum a concilio sancto curae committitur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p95","Incipit Edictum Regis in Confirmatione Concilii.","The most glorious lord Recared the king. The divine truth of all under the governance of our power consisting, lovers of you, making our principal senses to inspire, that for the sake of restoring the faith and ecclesiastical discipline all the bishops of Spain to our summit we should order to be presented. A diligent and cautious deliberation preceding, both those things which to the faith agree and those which to the correction of customs look, by maturity of sense and by gravity of understanding we have established to be digested. Our authority therefore by this to all men to our kingdom pertaining commands, that, if any things have been defined in this holy council held in the city of Toledo in the fourth year of our reign happily, to none is it permitted to despise, let no one presume to pass over. The chapters indeed, which to our senses pleasing and to discipline congruent by this synod have been written down, in all authority both of clerics or of all whoever let them be observed and remain, that is: concerning the observation of the prior canons; concerning the symbol to be brought forth by the peoples in the church; concerning bishops, that it not be lawful for them the property of the church to alienate; that it be lawful for a bishop one of the parish churches a monastery to make; that to bishops and presbyters and deacons from heresy converted it no longer be lawful to be mingled with wives, or that those who have always been catholic in their cells with extraneous women not remain; that freedmen by bishops or by others made and to churches commended to remain free ought; that reading in all priestly tables ought to be read; that clerics from the families of our fisc no one ever from the king request, and whoever shall have received, let such a donation remain void; concerning churches from heresy transferred to the bishops in whose parishes they are, let them pertain; concerning widows, that those which shall have willed, let them hold continence, and those which shall have chosen to marry, to whom they shall have willed, let them marry, similarly concerning virgins; that penitents according to the manner of the ancient canons ought to do penance; that those who shall have willed to do penance first be tonsured or change the habit; that it not be lawful for Jews to take from Christians wives or concubines or to purchase Christian slaves, and it not be lawful to Judaize or public offices to perform; that remain firm, if slaves of our fisc churches shall have made and them from their own peculium shall have dowered; that the worship of idolatry by priests and judges be searched out and exterminated; that those who shall have killed their son, by priests and by judges be constrained; that once in a year to the council the priests and judges and actors of our patrimony ought to convene; that the cause of all churches to the ordinance of the bishop ought to pertain; that priests moderately ought to act through the parishes; that the slaves of the church or of clerics ought not by judges or by our actors in any angary to be fatigued; that the bodies of the religious with hymns and songs only are to be carried to the sepulchers; that dances and turpid songs are to be prohibited from the solemnities of the saints.","Gloriosissimus dominus Recaredus rex universorum sub regimine nostrae potestatis consistentium amatores vestri divina faciens veritas nostris principaliter sensibus inspiravit, ut causa instaurandae fidei ac disciplinae ecclesiasticae episcopos omnes Hispaniae nostro praesentari culmini iuberemus. Praecedente autem diligenti et cauta deliberatione, sive quae ad fidem conveniant seu quae ad morum correctionem respiciunt, sensus maturitate et intelligentiae gravitate constant esse digesta. Nostra proinde auctoritas hac omnibus hominibus ad regnum nostrum pertinentibus iubet, ut, si qua definita sunt in hoc sancto concilio acto in urbe Toletana anno regni nostri feliciter quarto, nulli contemnere liceat, nullus praeterire praesumat. Capitula enim, quae sensibus nostris placita et disciplinae congrua a praesenti conscripta sunt synodo, in omni auctoritate sive clericorum sive quorumcumque omnium observentur et maneant, id est: de observatione priorum canonum; de symbolo proferendo a populis in ecclesia; de episcopis, ut eis non liceat rem alienare ecclesiae; ut episcopo liceat unam de parrochitanis ecclesiis monasterium facere; ut episcopis et presbyteris et diaconibus ex heresi conversis iam non liceat misceri uxoribus, vel quod hi, qui semper catholici fuerint, in cellulis suis cum mulieribus extraneis non morentur; quod liberti ab episcopis vel aliis facti et ecclesiis commendati permanere debeant liberi; quod lectio in omnibus sacerdotalibus mensis legi debeat; quod clericos ex familiis fisci nostri nullus umquam a rege postulet, et qui acceperit, irrita talis donatio maneat; de ecclesiis ab heresi translatis ad episcopos, in quorum sunt parrochiis, pertineant; de viduis, quod, quae voluerint, continentiam teneant, et quae nubere elegerint, quibus voluerint, nubant, aeque de virginibus; quod poenitentes secundum modum canonum antiquorum debeant agere poenitentiam; quod qui voluerint poenitentiam agere prius tondantur aut habitum mutent; quod non liceat Iudaeis ducere de christianis uxores vel concubinas sive comparare mancipia christiana et iudaizare non liceat vel publica officia peragere; quod manere debeat firmum, si servi fisci nostri ecclesias fecerint easque de peculio suo dotaverint; quod idolatriae cultum a sacerdotibus vel iudicibus exquirenda sit atque exterminanda; quod quae filium suum necaverint, a sacerdotibus vel a iudicibus distringantur; quod semel in anno ad concilium sacerdotes et iudices atque actores patrimonii nostri debeant convenire; quod ecclesiarum omnium causa ad episcopi ordinationem pertinere debeat; quod sacerdotes moderanter agere debeant per parrochias; quod servi ecclesiae sive clericorum non debeant a iudicibus vel nostris actoribus in aliqua angaria fatigari; quod religiosorum corpora cum hymnis et canticis tantum deferenda sint ad sepulchra; quod ballimathiae et turpia cantica prohibenda sunt a sanctorum sollemniis."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p96","Incipit Edictum Regis in Confirmatione Concilii.","All these ecclesiastical constitutions, which summarily and briefly we have run through, just as more fully in the canon are contained, to remain with perpetual stability we sanction. If therefore any cleric or layman of these sanctions to be obedient shall have been unwilling, if a bishop, presbyter, deacon, or cleric shall have been, from all council to excommunication let him be subject; if indeed a layman shall have been and of a more honorable place the person is, the half of his goods let him lose, to the fisc's forces to profit; if indeed of a lesser place the person is, by the loss of his goods punished, into exile let him be assigned.","Has omnes constitutiones ecclesiasticas, quas summatim breviterque perstrinximus, sicut plenius in canone continentur, manere perenni stabilitate sancimus. Si quis ergo clericus aut laicus harum sanctionum oboediens esse noluerit, si episcopus, presbyter, diaconus aut clericus fuerit, ab omni concilio excommunicationi subiaceat, si vero laicus fuerit et honestioris loci persona est, medietatem facultatum suarum amittat fisci viribus profuturam. Si vero minoris loci persona est, amissione rerum suarum multatus in exilium deputetur."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p97","Incipit Edictum Regis in Confirmatione Concilii.","Flavius Recared the king this deliberation, which with the holy synod we have defined, confirming I have subscribed.","Flavius Recaredus rex hanc deliberationem, quam cum sancta definivimus synodo, confirmans subscripsi."],["vol3/toledo-iii/index.html","p98","Incipit Edictum Regis in Confirmatione Concilii.","Masona in the name of Christ of the catholic church of Merida metropolitan bishop of the province of Lusitania to these constitutions which in the city of Toledo I was present, with my hand I have subscribed. Similarly also the other bishops subscribed, that is 68.","Masona in Christi nomine ecclesiae catholicae Emeretensis metropolitanus episcopus provinciae Lusitaniae eis constitutionibus quibus in urbe Toletana interfui, manu mea subscripsi. Similiter et alii episcopi subscripserunt, id est LXVIII."]];